│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dynamic_repair_swap                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This approach keeps the input graph as the initial state, repairs it using an             │
│                          │ incrementally maintained common-neighbor matrix, and then performs degree-balanced        │
│                          │ saturation. Unlike the original one-pass repair, every deletion is chosen to eliminate    │
│                          │ many current C4 violations. After reaching a valid C4-free graph, it repeatedly adds the  │
│                          │ legal non-edge with the best degree-balancing score.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It then applies several bounded “destroy and refill” local-search rounds: remove a few    │
│                          │ highly blocking edges, greedily refill the resulting gaps, and retain the best valid      │
│                          │ graph found. All additions are checked through the invariant that every off-diagonal      │
│                          │ entry of the common-neighbor matrix remains at most one. A final explicit                 │
│                          │ validation-and-repair pass is included for safety.                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0660                                                                                   │
