│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ balanced_c4_local_search                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This version repairs the input graph by greedily retaining a C4-free subset of its        │
│                          │ original edges, then performs balanced saturation using the characterization that adding  │
│                          │ an edge is valid exactly when its endpoints have no length-three path between them.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Several input-dependent repair orders are tried. The best repaired graph is then improved │
│                          │ through a small number of delete-and-refill perturbations: deleting a few high-degree     │
│                          │ edges can unlock several new valid edges. Every candidate is explicitly checked using the │
│                          │ common-neighbor invariant, and a conservative repair fallback is included before          │
│                          │ returning.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The algorithm never substitutes a hard-coded construction: all edge priorities, repair    │
│                          │ choices, and perturbations are derived from the supplied adjacency matrix and RNG.        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
