│ patch_name               │ balanced_multistart_swap                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses 3 input-repair orders, a blocked-cost saturation score of `4 *  │
│                          │ blocked_cost + degree_sum`, and 9 delete/refill trials. The new version keeps the same    │
│                          │ input-dependent repair principle but changes the search configuration:                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Uses 4 distinct input-retention orders, including endpoint-load, dense-region, random,  │
│                          │ and degree-product orders.                                                                │
│                          │ - Uses a more balance-sensitive saturation score `3 * blocked_cost + 2 * degree_sum`,     │
│                          │ encouraging near-regular dense C4-free graphs instead of over-prioritizing short-term     │
│                          │ blocking cost.                                                                            │
│                          │ - Uses 14 bounded perturbation trials with adaptive deletion sizes of 2, 3, and 4 edges.  │
│                          │ - Allows controlled equal-quality moves so that the search can leave one saturated local  │
│                          │ optimum and discover a different one.                                                     │
│                          │ - Keeps all construction stages C4-safe using the length-three-path test, and explicitly  │
│                          │ verifies the common-neighbor invariant before returning.                                  │
│                          │ - Uses only edits derived from the supplied adjacency matrix: retained input edges form   │
│                          │ every initial state, then additions/deletions improve those states.                       │
