│ patch_name               │ beam_ruin_refill                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This version uses a multi-start repair phase followed by a small beam-style               │
│                          │ ruin-and-refill search. It still starts from the supplied adjacency matrix and only       │
│                          │ modifies it through deletions and safe additions.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key difference is that it keeps several strong maximal C4-free states rather than     │
│                          │ following one local-search trajectory. Each round destroys a carefully selected set of    │
│                          │ high-blocking edges from several beam members, refills using a balanced bitset-based      │
│                          │ saturation rule, and retains the best diverse outcomes. This reduces sensitivity to       │
│                          │ unlucky repair and refill choices while preserving the mandatory invariant that every     │
│                          │ pair has at most one common neighbor.                                                     │
