│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ conflict_credit_exchange                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This version keeps the successful input-repair and safe-saturation ideas from the prior   │
│                          │ programs, but changes the escape mechanism into a conflict-credit exchange search.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The main additions are:                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Several genuinely input-derived repairs use complementary source-degree and             │
│                          │ source-product orderings.                                                                 │
│                          │ - Saturation scores legal insertions using both exact future blocking cost and a stronger │
│                          │ near-regular degree penalty.                                                              │
│                          │ - Instead of deleting merely high-degree edges, destructive moves prioritize edges with   │
│                          │ high conflict credit, approximately `(deg(u)-1)*(deg(v)-1)`. Such edges are central to    │
│                          │ many blocked length-three paths, so removing them is more likely to unlock several new    │
│                          │ edges.                                                                                    │
│                          │ - A compact elite archive keeps several structurally different saturated graphs rather    │
│                          │ than only one incumbent.                                                                  │
│                          │ - Deleted edges are temporarily banned during refill, forcing genuine exchanges before    │
│                          │ allowing restoration.                                                                     │
│                          │ - Every repair, exchange, and final result is explicitly checked using the                │
│                          │ common-neighbor characterization of C4-freeness.                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
