│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ unlock_kick_archive                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The previous archive search used 6 repair starts, a `3 * future_loss + 2 * degree_load`   │
│                          │ insertion score, and destructive kicks chosen primarily from high-degree endpoint         │
│                          │ pressure. Its main weakness is that high-degree edges are not necessarily the edges       │
│                          │ preventing useful replacements.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version keeps the input-derived repair and archive architecture, but changes the     │
│                          │ local-search configuration as follows:                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Uses 5 source-dependent repair orders plus more diverse tie-breaking.                   │
│                          │ - Changes saturation scoring to `4 * future_loss + degree_load`, making preservation of   │
│                          │ future legal pairs primary while still avoiding hubs.                                     │
│                          │ - Keeps a larger archive of 6 structurally distinct maximal graphs.                       │
│                          │ - Replaces pressure-only deletions with an explicit *unlock score*: for each existing     │
│                          │ edge, estimate how many currently forbidden nonedges become legal if that edge is removed │
│                          │ because it is the unique length-three path blocking them.                                 │
│                          │ - Uses 18 bounded two-to-four-edge kicks. Kicks select edges with high unlock score, with │
│                          │ degree pressure only as a secondary criterion.                                            │
│                          │ - Deleted edges remain temporarily banned during refill, forcing genuinely different      │
│                          │ structures before old edges can return.                                                   │
│                          │ - Every insertion is checked locally, every phase is checked using the common-neighbor    │
│                          │ characterization, and final monotone repair remains defensive.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key new parameters are `LOSS_WEIGHT=4`, `LOAD_WEIGHT=1`, archive size `6`, source-tie │
│                          │ preference `0.35`, and the 18-kick schedule with adaptive deletion sizes and exploration  │
│                          │ percentiles.                                                                              │
