│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses five source-repair styles, a matrix-cube-based saturation       │
│                          │ routine, a four-state archive, and fourteen exchange moves with removals of two to four   │
│                          │ edges. Its strongest components are source-dependent repairs and banned-edge refill       │
│                          │ exchanges, but repeated dense matrix multiplications make it expensive to explore many    │
│                          │ trajectories.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version replaces repeated `A @ A @ A` legality computations with exact Python        │
│                          │ integer bitset tests. An insertion `uv` is accepted only when no neighbor of `u` is       │
│                          │ adjacent to a neighbor of `v`, exactly preserving the C4-free invariant. The faster       │
│                          │ legality test permits a broader search configuration: five source-derived starts, a       │
│                          │ five-state archive, and twenty bounded ruin-and-refill exchanges. Saturation prioritizes  │
│                          │ balanced degrees around 6--7, lightly favors supplied input edges, and randomizes         │
│                          │ near-tied choices. Exchange removals target high degree-product edges while preferring    │
│                          │ disjoint deletions, then temporarily ban removed edges so refill is encouraged to find    │
│                          │ genuine replacements rather than immediately undoing the move.                            │
