│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ pathincidence_archive                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This version keeps the input-aware repair-and-augment framework, but replaces the         │
│                          │ previous deletion heuristic with an exact obstruction-incidence score.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For every currently blocked missing edge `x-y` having exactly one length-three path       │
│                          │ `x-a-b-y`, the algorithm credits all three edges of that path: `x-a`, `a-b`, and `b-y`.   │
│                          │ Deleting any one of these edges unlocks `x-y`, so destructive moves are selected from     │
│                          │ edges that participate in many unique obstructions rather than only treating the middle   │
│                          │ edge of a path as useful.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search uses several source-derived repairs, plus a small number of source-biased      │
│                          │ neutral completions from an empty edit state. All constructions remain guided by the      │
│                          │ supplied matrix through edge-retention orders and tie-breaking preferences. Each          │
│                          │ candidate is greedily saturated using a future-loss score, then archive-based             │
│                          │ obstruction-targeted ruin/refill moves search for improvements. Every addition is guarded │
│                          │ by the C4 invariant and final validation is explicit.                                     │
