│ patch_description        │ This version restores a stronger input-aware repair-and-refill strategy. It begins from   │
│                          │ the supplied adjacency matrix, repeatedly deletes edges that participate in the largest   │
│                          │ number of common-neighbor violations, then greedily saturates the repaired graph using    │
│                          │ exact bitset C4 tests.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Several independently tie-broken repairs are retained in a small beam. Each beam state is │
│                          │ subjected to bounded ruin-and-refill moves that delete structurally expensive edges and   │
│                          │ greedily refill using balanced low-degree endpoint choices. Every addition is checked     │
│                          │ using the exact condition that no edge may connect the two endpoint neighborhoods. Every  │
│                          │ major phase also explicitly verifies the common-neighbor invariant before accepting a     │
│                          │ candidate.                                                                                │
