│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exact_unlock_archive                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program lost performance mainly because its `unlock_scores` routine evaluates │
│                          │ each present edge independently with nested neighborhood loops, while its saturation      │
│                          │ modes over-emphasize degree-six balancing. This replacement restores the stronger exact   │
│                          │ obstruction-incidence scoring used by the best prior archive approach: every missing pair │
│                          │ with one unique length-three path credits all three edges on that path, so deletions are  │
│                          │ selected based on directly unlocked insertions.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key configuration changes:                                                                │
│                          │ - `ARCHIVE_LIMIT = 10` instead of 8, preserving more distinct high-quality basins.        │
│                          │ - Six full input-derived repairs plus four bounded input-derived scaffolds, rather than   │
│                          │ relying only on full repairs.                                                             │
│                          │ - Saturation uses future legal-edge loss as the dominant criterion (`4 * loss + load`),   │
│                          │ with only mild degree balancing.                                                          │
│                          │ - Source-edge preference is retained as a tie bias (`0.40`) so the graph is genuinely     │
│                          │ edited from the supplied input.                                                           │
│                          │ - 24 bounded delete/refill kicks use exact unique-obstruction credits and temporary edge  │
│                          │ bans.                                                                                     │
│                          │ - Every scaffold, refill state, archive insertion, and final state is explicitly checked  │
│                          │ for the C4-free invariant.                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
