│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ path_unlock_archive                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This version uses a path-obstruction archive search. It first extracts multiple C4-free   │
│                          │ scaffolds directly from differently ordered subsets of the input graph, including         │
│                          │ deliberately bounded source-derived scaffolds that avoid inheriting dense bad regions too │
│                          │ early. Each scaffold is saturated by selecting legal insertions that minimize the number  │
│                          │ of remaining legal edges destroyed.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For local improvement, it scores deletable edges by the number of uniquely blocked        │
│                          │ length-three paths that use them. Removing such an edge makes several currently forbidden │
│                          │ pairs potentially legal, so delete/refill kicks are targeted at genuine C4 obstructions   │
│                          │ rather than simply high-degree edges. Every insertion is checked locally, every candidate │
│                          │ is validated through the common-neighbor characterization, and final repair is            │
│                          │ deletion-only if required.                                                                │
