│ patch_name               │ repair_tabu_balance                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program relies only on source-edge greedy starts and uses a relatively        │
│                          │ restrictive scalar saturation score, which produced lower mean density than the earlier   │
│                          │ repair-based approach. This version restores conflict-directed repair of the actual input │
│                          │ graph, combines it with source-preserving greedy starts, and uses balanced lexicographic  │
│                          │ saturation with a soft source-edge tie preference.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key configuration changes:                                                                │
│                          │ - **4 conflict-directed repairs**: delete edges that cover many current C4 violations     │
│                          │ before augmentation.                                                                      │
│                          │ - **4 source-preserving constructive starts**: retain different valid subsets of the      │
│                          │ input graph.                                                                              │
│                          │ - **Archive size 4** rather than 5, concentrating exchange search on stronger candidates. │
│                          │ - **14 tabu ruin-and-refill moves** with deletion sizes 2–6.                              │
│                          │ - **Balanced saturation key**: prioritize low total degree, then penalize degrees above   │
│                          │ 7, then degree product.                                                                   │
│                          │ - **Tabu refill** prevents immediately restoring deleted edges until alternative          │
│                          │ additions have been attempted.                                                            │
│                          │ - Every archive insertion and final result explicitly verifies the common-neighbor        │
│                          │ invariant.                                                                                │
