│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_bitset_ruin                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses 8 initial states, a 4-state archive, 12 tabu ruin rounds,       │
│                          │ degree-first saturation, and deletion scores based mainly on endpoint degree products.    │
│                          │ The new configuration keeps the input-derived repair and source-preserving starts, but    │
│                          │ changes the search balance:                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Uses 6 conflict-directed repairs and 5 source-preserving greedy starts with more        │
│                          │ diverse edge-retention orders.                                                            │
│                          │ - Uses bitset-safe insertion tests throughout, preserving the C4-free invariant after     │
│                          │ every edge addition.                                                                      │
│                          │ - Adds adaptive saturation modes: strongly balanced degree growth, degree-product         │
│                          │ minimization, and mixed regularity/product selection.                                     │
│                          │ - Expands the elite archive to 6 structurally distinct candidates.                        │
│                          │ - Uses 18 controlled ruin-and-refill moves, with 2–6 deleted edges and tabu protection    │
│                          │ against immediately restoring deleted edges.                                              │
│                          │ - Uses a stronger “unlocking” deletion score based on the number of cross-neighborhood    │
│                          │ pairs blocked by an edge, rather than only degree pressure.                               │
│                          │ - Retains explicit matrix validation after every major phase and before return.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The principal changed parameters are `INITIAL_REPAIRS=6`, `INITIAL_GREEDY=5`,             │
│                          │ `ARCHIVE_LIMIT=6`, and an 18-step adaptive kick schedule. Saturation now mixes three      │
│                          │ degree-selection configurations rather than relying on one fixed degree-first ordering.   │
