│ patch_description        │ The current program uses five source-retention starts, a four-state archive, and fourteen │
│                          │ single-base exchange trials. Its saturation score heavily weights matrix-computed         │
│                          │ future-loss estimates, which can become overly greedy and produces relatively weak mean   │
│                          │ density (146.94).                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version uses a bitset representation for much faster safe-edge testing, allowing a   │
│                          │ broader search configuration: four conflict-directed repairs, four constructive           │
│                          │ source-preserving starts, a four-member elite archive, and a tabu ruin-and-refill beam.   │
│                          │ Each exchange round evaluates the best several archive members rather than only one       │
│                          │ selected base. Removed edges are temporarily taboo during refill, forcing the search to   │
│                          │ exploit newly unlocked edges instead of immediately restoring the deleted edges.          │
│                          │ Saturation prioritizes lower endpoint degree/load, with an explicit target degree near    │
│                          │ 6--7, which is more consistent with dense near-regular C4-free graphs on 49 vertices.     │
│                          │ Every generated candidate is explicitly checked using the common-neighbor criterion       │
│                          │ before archive insertion and before return.                                               │
