│ patch_description        │ This version combines conflict-directed repair with a new pair-budget guided refill       │
│                          │ strategy.  It treats a C4-free graph as a resource allocation problem: every new edge     │
│                          │ consumes potential cross-neighborhood pairs, so saturation prioritizes low-degree         │
│                          │ endpoint pairs while avoiding excessive degree concentration.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The algorithm remains genuinely input-dependent. It begins from several differently       │
│                          │ repaired versions of the supplied adjacency matrix and from several source-edge retention │
│                          │ orders. Each valid candidate is saturated using safe bitset additions. A small archive is │
│                          │ then improved through tabu ruin-and-refill moves: high-pressure edges are deleted         │
│                          │ temporarily, their immediate re-addition is forbidden, and the newly opened space is      │
│                          │ refilled using balanced safe additions. Every completed candidate is explicitly verified  │
│                          │ using the common-neighbor characterization of C4-freeness.                                │
