│ patch_description        │ The current augmentation penalizes every endpoint degree above six, despite dense C4-free │
│                          │ graphs on 49 vertices typically requiring many degree-seven vertices to reach the best    │
│                          │ edge counts. The ordinary endpoint-load term already discourages excessive hubs. Moving   │
│                          │ the explicit excess penalty threshold to seven allows useful seventh incident edges while │
│                          │ retaining a stronger penalty once degree eight is reached. This only changes the ranking  │
│                          │ of already legal insertions; the C4-free invariant and all explicit validation remain     │
│                          │ untouched.                                                                                │
