│ patch_description        │ Restore a larger elite archive and a longer, more varied ruin-and-refill schedule. Dense  │
│                          │ C4-free graphs commonly sit behind multi-edge saturation barriers: deleting only two or   │
│                          │ three edges may refill to the same maximal graph, whereas occasional 5--6 edge moves can  │
│                          │ reach a different degree distribution and then gain edges after refill. Retaining six     │
│                          │ archive states also prevents the search from repeatedly exploring only the current best   │
│                          │ basin.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is still fully input-aware: every base state comes from repairing or greedily        │
│                          │ retaining edges from the supplied matrix, and every proposal is produced by deleting and  │
│                          │ adding edges to those states. Validity remains preserved because deletions cannot create  │
│                          │ C4s and all refill additions use `legal_add`, followed by explicit `valid` checks.        │
