│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It builds multiple C4-free subsets of the supplied input edges using degree-based and     │
│                          │ randomized source orders. Each scaffold is saturated using a legal insertion rule based   │
│                          │ on the no-common-neighbor characterization. Saturation scores insertions by estimated     │
│                          │ future candidate loss, degree balance, and source-edge preference.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Compared with the previous version, the archive is larger and local search includes       │
│                          │ targeted one-edge, medium, and larger obstruction-aware deletion phases. Larger removals  │
│                          │ can escape locally maximal C4-free configurations that cannot be improved by only         │
│                          │ removing two or three edges. All inserted states are explicitly validated, and final      │
│                          │ repair is deletion-only if needed.                                                        │
