│ patch_description        │ This rewrite replaces repeated matrix-cube saturation with a faster bitset-based C4-safe  │
│                          │ insertion engine. It keeps the input graph relevant by building multiple                  │
│                          │ source-edge-derived scaffolds under several orderings and bounded prefixes, then augments │
│                          │ them using safe additions.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For each candidate insertion, the algorithm explicitly checks the C4 condition: adding uv │
│                          │ is allowed only when no current edge joins N(u) and N(v). It estimates the number of      │
│                          │ future edges blocked by the insertion using the newly created length-three paths,         │
│                          │ preferring additions that preserve future flexibility and maintain balanced degrees.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A compact elite archive is improved using bounded ruin-and-refill exchanges.              │
│                          │ High-pressure edges are temporarily deleted, banned during the first refill phase, and    │
│                          │ replaced with alternative edges where possible. Every archived candidate is explicitly    │
│                          │ validated using A @ A, and the final result has a conservative repair fallback.           │
