│ patch_name               │ future_loss_saturation                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the degree-only saturation score with a C4-specific future-loss estimate.  When a │
│                          │ legal edge uv is inserted, it creates new length-three paths x-u-v-y for pairs x in N(u), │
│                          │ y in N(v).  Every currently legal missing pair xy of this form becomes unavailable        │
│                          │ afterwards.  Thus the number of legal cross-neighborhood pairs is a direct estimate of    │
│                          │ how many future insertions uv destroys.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The existing code already enumerates all legal insertions in every saturation iteration.  │
│                          │ This edit records those legal pairs as bit masks and scores each candidate using the      │
│                          │ exact current cross-neighborhood legal-pair count, while retaining balanced-degree        │
│                          │ secondary criteria and the source preference.  This should avoid early edges which        │
│                          │ rapidly consume the pair budget and improve the chance of reaching near-regular 154+ edge │
│                          │ maximal graphs.                                                                           │
