│ patch_description        │ The current program uses 6 repair starts, 5 source-greedy starts, a small archive of 6    │
│                          │ candidates, and degree-only saturation keys. Its main weakness is that degree balancing   │
│                          │ alone does not estimate how many legal future edges an insertion destroys.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version uses:                                                                        │
│                          │ - 4 conflict-directed repairs and 10 input-derived greedy scaffold starts.                │
│                          │ - Archive size increased from 6 to 8.                                                     │
│                          │ - A stronger saturation score based on exact length-three-path obstruction information.   │
│                          │ Candidate edges are scored by estimated future legal-edge loss, degree load, imbalance,   │
│                          │ and excessive degree pressure.                                                            │
│                          │ - 20 bounded ruin/refill moves with tabu-deleted edges.                                   │
│                          │ - Explicit C4 validation after every repair, saturation, and exchange phase.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key change is the obstruction-aware saturation policy: it favors legal additions      │
│                          │ which preserve more remaining legal pairs, rather than only selecting low-degree          │
│                          │ endpoints.                                                                                │
