│ patch_name               │ bitset_balanced_ejection                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This replaces repeated dense matrix-cube scoring with an incremental bitset-based search. │
│                          │ Each graph is represented by 49-bit neighborhood masks, so testing whether an insertion   │
│                          │ creates a C4 only requires checking whether any edge joins the two endpoint               │
│                          │ neighborhoods.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The algorithm builds several genuinely input-derived C4-free scaffolds using randomized   │
│                          │ source-edge priorities, then performs balanced greedy completion. Candidate insertions    │
│                          │ are chosen from all legal pairs using a degree-balancing score, with mild preference for  │
│                          │ edges present in the supplied input. A small elite archive is improved through            │
│                          │ high-pressure edge ejection moves: edges around overloaded vertices are removed,          │
│                          │ temporarily banned, and the graph is greedily refilled into a potentially denser basin.   │
│                          │ Every insertion is locally C4-safe, and final matrix validation is retained defensively.  │
